Can we add a `TODO` here for this? E.g.
```
// TODO: The matching attributes from the left and right logical plans should become part of the `expressions()`
// so that `references()` returns the attributes we actually rely on. Probably move them out of the JoinConfig
// and make them private attributes, instead.
```

Hm, what happens if neither left nor right are fragments, but contain fragments?

Also, I feel like this code is a bit over abstracted; we won't have general binary plans, because we cannot map them. We can only have a `Join` here, and only a left one with a local relation on the right.
I think this code would be simpler to read if we started with this assumption, or made it more prominent:
```java
if (p instanceof Join join) {
            if (join.config().type() != JoinType.LEFT) {
                throw new EsqlIllegalArgumentException("unsupported logical plan node [" + p.nodeName() + "]");
            }
            var left = map(bp.left());
            var right = map(bp.right());
           // check if mapping `left` results in a fragment
           //...
            if (rhs instanceof LocalSourceExec local) {
                return new HashJoinExec(local.source(), left, local, join.config().unionFields(), join.output());
            }
            throw new EsqlIllegalArgumentException("unsupported logical plan node [" + p.nodeName() + "]");
}
```
